            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Soooooo yummy. The only changes I made was substituting apple cider vinegar for red wine vinegar, canola oil for olive oil - less about 1 tablespoon, adding a tablespoon of toasted sesame oil, and adding about 1 tablespoon of chopped chives. Adding nutritional yeast will thicken it if you find it too thin, but I did not find that necessary. I thought the consistency was perfect the way it is. Very much like Goddess dressing."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jamie Underwood"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Amazing! I have been making tahini dressing since i was a kid and tried this with some of what i do in mine and it was a perfect harmony. I omitted the olive oil and used 1/4 c sesame oil instead. Then i added chopped green onion and a small handful of parsley. I used just a tad more lemon juice and garlic and cut back on the water by half, i like mine a little thicker. Thank you thank you!",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-20T17:47:08.377Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FizzySpoon2633"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Overall easy recipe and very good flavor. Will make again. I used Japanese rice wine vinegar instead of red wine vinegar (not a fan) and substituted 1 ounce (2 tablespoons) of olive oil with sesame oil to bring out the flavor of the tahini. I would do the same next time with the addition of increasing the lemon juice because I like the freshness of lemon.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-15T16:51:58.714Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sfhutch"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this dressing! Tasty, easy and healthy! I just dump everything, including whole peeled ginger and garlic in Vitamix and press the button.",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-22T10:28:44.840Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Max"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I will definitely make it again! No modification, except no blender. Simply whisked it with a spoon, and mashed the tahini lumps!",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-12T02:49:20.430Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Anoushka"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very mild. I added lots of ginger (at least 1.5 inch of root), an extra tbs of lemon juice and about 2 tbs of sesame oil (dark one). I used rice vinegar. I suggest to omit the water instead of adding all that stuff...",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-29T14:26:56.540Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Channing Quinn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Oh my god! This is so good! I added a little extra fresh ginger, twice the garlic, and a little extra tahini. It came out fantastic! I LOVE ginger and garlic so I absolutely did not find any of the flavors to be overpowering. :) I was surprised that anyone said it came out chalky. Maybe it depends on the quality of tahini paste you use. The tahini paste I used was not quite thick like peanut butter. A little more oily. Anyway, this is a new favorite around here! Will be making it again and again anytime I run out! And salads every day from now on. :D",
            "datePublished": "2016-09-16T17:23:49.293Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DOUGBENME"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The only change I made was apple cider vinegar because it was easier to reach in the pantry, and very little water because my tahini was already pretty thin. The flavors were just what I was looking for, reminiscent of the hibachi grill salad drawing. It was quick, easy, and honestly, you don't have to be very precise on ingredients. I loved how it clung to the lettuce and veggies in my salad. In the future, I may adapt it some to include red pepper or other spices, and to experiment with different vinegars and soy sauces. But I thought it was perfect just like it is.",
            "datePublished": "2025-06-07T16:58:12.586Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "abbiferris"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good start as is, but all I tasted was vinegar and soy. So, I added a teaspoon of orange zest, a couple of tablespoons of Splenda brown sugar and a dash or two of cayenne. Much better!",
            "datePublished": "2013-09-17T13:49:30.840Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Thompson Elizabeth"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It's delicious. I made a few substitutions for what I had at home: red wine vinegar-&gt; apple cider vinegar, tamari-&gt; liquid Aminos, olive oil-&gt; canola . I used juice of a whole lemon. I think I would put less water, it was a little too thin for my liking. Im definitely going to use it as a staple. It's very good. I recommend.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-02T16:16:37.870Z"
          },
          {
